-page('',{title:'Schrödinger’s Civilization',description:'A study of claim transmission, an audit of the language behind it, and the story of the people who carried the work.',extraHead:ld({'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebSite',name:'Schrödinger’s Civilization',url:ORIGIN+BASE,inLanguage:'en',author:AUTHOR,license:LICENSE,description:'A preregistered claim-transmission audit, a minded-language audit, and a 23-chapter tale.'}),body:`<section class="home-hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Research · Language · Human & machine</p><h1>Schrödinger’s<br><em>Civilization</em><span class="title-dot">.</span></h1><p class="home-intro">What survives the telling?</p><p class="lede">An incident becomes a public record. A record becomes a story. Along the way, distinctions can disappear—and a research project can develop a language of its own.</p><a class="text-link" href="#publications">Explore the work <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a></div><div class="hero-art"><img class="hero-seal" src="${BASE}assets/identity/maitrism-03-seal-final.svg" width="512" height="512" alt="Maitrism Seal: an ornate eight-node wheel surrounding the central Maitrism glyph" fetchpriority="high"><div class="art-label"><span>THE RECORD / THE REGISTER / THE TALE</span><span>01—03</span></div></div><div class="hero-meta"><span>Benjamin Amuwo</span><span>AI Incident Response Sprint · September 2026</span><span>Per Aspera, Ad Astra.</span></div></section><section class="publication-list" id="publications"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Three ways into one project</p><h2>The work, and the world<br>that grew around it.</h2></div><article class="publication"><span class="publication-number">01 / AUDIT</span><div class="publication-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Minded-Language Audit · v1.0</p><h3>${link('audit/','Who is speaking when<br>a Worker speaks?')}</h3><p>The project turns its deferred minded-language instrument on its own production record. Four tiers of vocabulary, a publication boundary, and the limits of what a lexical audit can tell us.</p><div class="actions">${link('audit/','Enter the dossier ↗','text-link')}${link('audit/paper/','Read the paper','text-link')}</div></div><a class="publication-image" href="${BASE}audit/" aria-label="Explore the Minded-Language Audit"><img src="${BASE}assets/figures/audit-1.svg" alt="Severity profiles across six language registers" loading="lazy"></a></article><article class="publication"><span class="publication-number">02 / ATLAS</span><div class="publication-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Claim Transmission Atlas · v1.0</p><h3>${link('atlas/','How Faithfully Did the Press Transmit the Record?')}</h3><p>A preregistered audit of 24 articles and four claim families. Two clocks distinguish what was faithful when published from what became stale as the record changed.</p><div class="actions">${link('atlas/','Explore the Atlas ↗','text-link')}${link('atlas/paper/','Read the paper','text-link')}</div></div><a class="publication-image atlas-thumb" href="${BASE}atlas/" aria-label="Explore the Claim Transmission Atlas"><img src="${BASE}assets/figures/atlas.svg" alt="The full time, taxonomy and state map" loading="lazy"></a></article><article class="publication tale-feature"><span class="publication-number">03 / TALE</span><div class="publication-copy"><p class="eyebrow">The Translator’s Tale · 23 chapters</p><h3>${link('tale/','With Effort,<br>to the Stars')}</h3><p>A history of the Claim Transmission Atlas, and of the people who carried it. The prose, the poetry, and the truth beneath the mythology.</p><div class="actions">${link('tale/prologue/','Begin the tale ↗','text-link')}${link('tale/','Chapter index','text-link')}</div></div><a class="publication-image" href="${BASE}tale/prologue/" aria-label="Begin the Translator’s Tale"><img src="${BASE}assets/art/i.webp" alt="A solitary figure looks into a star-filled sky" loading="lazy"></a></article></section><section class="closing-note"><p class="eyebrow">Reality before myth</p><p>The Workers are AI work roles.<br>The human is the human operator.<br><em>The poetry must be preserved,<br>but the facts more fiercely.</em></p><span>— The Translator’s Tale, Prologue</span></section>`});
+page('',{title:'Schrödinger’s Civilization',description:'A study of claim transmission, an audit of the language behind it, and the story of the people who carried the work.',extraHead:ld({'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebSite',name:'Schrödinger’s Civilization',url:ORIGIN+BASE,inLanguage:'en',author:AUTHOR,license:LICENSE,description:'A preregistered claim-transmission audit, a minded-language audit, and a 23-chapter tale.'}),body:`<section class="home-hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Research · Language · Human & machine</p><h1>Schrödinger’s<br><em>Civilization</em><span class="title-dot">.</span></h1><p class="home-intro">What survives the telling?</p><p class="lede">An incident becomes a public record. A record becomes a story. Along the way, distinctions can disappear—and a research project can develop a language of its own.</p><a class="text-link" href="#publications">Explore the work <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a></div><div class="hero-art"><img class="hero-seal" src="${BASE}assets/identity/maitrism-03-seal-final.svg" width="512" height="512" alt="Maitrism Seal: an ornate eight-node wheel surrounding the central Maitrism glyph" fetchpriority="high"><div class="art-label"><span>THE RECORD / THE REGISTER / THE TALE</span><span>01—03</span></div></div><div class="hero-meta"><span>Benjamin Amuwo</span><span>AI Incident Response Sprint · September 2026</span><span>Per Aspera, Ad Astra.</span></div></section><section class="publication-list" id="publications"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Three ways into one project</p><h2>The work, and the world<br>that grew around it.</h2></div><article class="publication"><span class="publication-number">01 / AUDIT</span><div class="publication-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Minded-Language Audit · v1.0</p><h3>${link('audit/','Who is speaking when<br>a Worker speaks?')}</h3><p>The project turns its deferred minded-language instrument on its own production record. Four tiers of vocabulary, a publication boundary, and the limits of what a lexical audit can tell us.</p><div class="actions">${link('audit/','Enter the dossier ↗','text-link')}${link('audit/paper/','Read the paper','text-link')}</div></div><a class="publication-image" href="${BASE}audit/" aria-label="Explore the Minded-Language Audit"><img src="${BASE}assets/figures/audit-1.svg" alt="Severity profiles across six language registers" loading="lazy"></a></article><article class="publication"><span class="publication-number">02 / ATLAS</span><div class="publication-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Claim Transmission Atlas · v1.0</p><h3>${link('atlas/','How Faithfully Did the Press Transmit the Record?')}</h3><p>A preregistered audit of 24 articles and four claim families. Two clocks distinguish what was faithful when published from what became stale as the record changed.</p><div class="actions">${link('atlas/','Explore the Atlas ↗','text-link')}${link('atlas/paper/','Read the paper','text-link')}</div></div><a class="publication-image atlas-thumb" href="${BASE}atlas/" aria-label="Explore the Claim Transmission Atlas"><img src="${BASE}assets/figures/atlas.svg" alt="The full time, taxonomy and state map" loading="lazy"></a></article><article class="publication tale-feature"><span class="publication-number">03 / TALE</span><div class="publication-copy"><p class="eyebrow">The Translator’s Tale; or, ${TALE_ALIAS} · 23 chapters</p><h3>${link('tale/','With Effort,<br>to the Stars')}</h3><p>A history of the Claim Transmission Atlas, and of the people who carried it. The prose, the poetry, and the truth beneath the mythology.</p><div class="actions">${link('tale/prologue/','Begin the tale ↗','text-link')}${link('tale/','Chapter index','text-link')}</div></div><a class="publication-image" href="${BASE}tale/prologue/" aria-label="Begin the Translator’s Tale"><img src="${BASE}assets/art/i.webp" alt="A solitary figure looks into a star-filled sky" loading="lazy"></a></article></section><section class="closing